1
00:00:00,336 --> 00:00:01,636
Please enjoy.

2
00:00:03,476 --> 00:00:04,976
Please, go ahead and eat.

3
00:00:07,020 --> 00:00:09,860
It's been a while since we went out to eat together.

4
00:00:10,490 --> 00:00:11,930
It's nice having Eun Seol here, too.

5
00:00:18,729 --> 00:00:19,729
Hold on.

6
00:00:20,429 --> 00:00:23,069
Eun Seol, can you not eat eggs?

7
00:00:26,499 --> 00:00:29,499
I'm allergic to egg whites.

8
00:00:29,569 --> 00:00:31,309
I haven't been able to eat them since I was little.

9
00:00:33,639 --> 00:00:34,679
Oh my.

10
00:00:35,039 --> 00:00:36,509
Me too.

11
00:00:36,979 --> 00:00:38,879
I'm also allergic to egg whites,

12
00:00:38,949 --> 00:00:41,619
so I haven't eaten eggs since I was young.

13
00:00:43,389 --> 00:00:45,519
We have quite a lot in common.

14
00:00:47,389 --> 00:00:48,489
I find it delicious.

15
00:00:56,029 --> 00:00:58,099
How's that something to bond over?

16
00:00:58,369 --> 00:01:00,139
It's just like atopic dermatitis.

17
00:01:00,339 --> 00:01:02,369
I couldn't eat eggs in the past, either.

18
00:01:02,439 --> 00:01:03,569
Couldn't eat them?

19
00:01:03,639 --> 00:01:05,809
We practically ran out because you ate them all.

20
00:01:14,619 --> 00:01:15,619
By the way,

21
00:01:17,119 --> 00:01:18,519
you said you studied design...

22
00:01:19,549 --> 00:01:21,619
at that place, right?

23
00:01:22,959 --> 00:01:24,859
Yes, that's right.

24
00:01:25,429 --> 00:01:28,429
I learned it through a prison vocational training program.

25
00:01:31,329 --> 00:01:34,169
I heard you even got a certification.

26
00:01:35,569 --> 00:01:38,109
Yes, I completed it as part of social rehabilitation.

27
00:01:40,679 --> 00:01:43,049
That is truly impressive.

28
00:01:43,649 --> 00:01:46,719
Very impressive. Something to be proud of, for sure.

29
00:01:58,329 --> 00:02:00,799
Aren't you engaged to Ms. Kang?

30
00:02:03,599 --> 00:02:05,099
Don't shake Eun Seol up...

31
00:02:05,869 --> 00:02:07,139
with your half-hearted sympathy.

32
00:02:08,899 --> 00:02:11,639
In the end, it will only hurt her.

33
00:02:13,039 --> 00:02:15,779
It seems to me like you're the one rattling her...

34
00:02:16,309 --> 00:02:18,049
just to ease your own guilt.

35
00:02:19,309 --> 00:02:20,749
At least I'm sincere.

36
00:02:21,749 --> 00:02:24,149
It's not a fleeting feeling like yours.

37
00:02:45,139 --> 00:02:46,779
Eating with Ko Eun Seol for no reason?

38
00:02:46,839 --> 00:02:48,609
It makes my stomach turn.

39
00:02:49,079 --> 00:02:50,679
She's your subordinate.

40
00:02:51,049 --> 00:02:52,449
Can't you be a little nicer to her?

41
00:02:53,779 --> 00:02:56,419
Mom, how could I possibly be nice to her?

42
00:02:57,589 --> 00:03:00,459
Don't tell me you've forgotten what she did to me in high school.

43
00:03:01,719 --> 00:03:03,089
Even ill fate is still fate.

44
00:03:03,629 --> 00:03:07,299
Seeing how tangled up you two are, it's no ordinary connection.

45
00:03:08,299 --> 00:03:12,129
Treat her well. Eun Seol has had a pitiful life.

46
00:03:12,699 --> 00:03:14,299
You actually feel sorry for her?

47
00:03:14,999 --> 00:03:16,909
She gives me the creeps.

48
00:03:17,209 --> 00:03:18,709
Whatever. This is so annoying.

49
00:03:19,269 --> 00:03:20,279
But...

50
00:03:23,509 --> 00:03:27,249
I wish our Hae Ra were as strong as Eun Seol.

51
00:03:29,249 --> 00:03:33,459
Eun Seol is a rare find these days, a truly upright person.

52
00:03:35,089 --> 00:03:36,089
Is that so?

53
00:03:37,289 --> 00:03:41,199
And surprisingly, we have a lot in common.

54
00:03:41,799 --> 00:03:42,959
Our tastes,

55
00:03:43,729 --> 00:03:46,099
and even the allergies we have. It's pretty fascinating.

56
00:03:46,999 --> 00:03:49,539
There are a lot of people with egg allergies these days.

57
00:03:50,239 --> 00:03:52,769
It must be the environment. It seems more common than before.

58
00:03:53,509 --> 00:03:55,809
Oh, really? I didn't know that.

59
00:04:04,719 --> 00:04:06,189
(Cheongma)

60
00:04:06,989 --> 00:04:10,529
With your inauguration as Chairman of Cheongma Scholarship Foundation,

61
00:04:10,589 --> 00:04:12,129
your fans are expressing disappointment.

62
00:04:12,589 --> 00:04:14,629
Should we view this move...

63
00:04:14,699 --> 00:04:17,969
as your complete retirement from acting?

64
00:04:18,329 --> 00:04:20,639
Well, I'm not sure. Retirement?

65
00:04:21,599 --> 00:04:24,569
If I ever come across a good project,

66
00:04:25,039 --> 00:04:28,239
I'll stand before my fans as actress Kim Jung Sun.

67
00:04:29,209 --> 00:04:30,409
But for now,

68
00:04:30,779 --> 00:04:33,449
I think it's time to focus on the foundation's work.

69
00:04:34,819 --> 00:04:38,319
Do you have a scholarship program in mind?

70
00:04:40,759 --> 00:04:43,089
Beyond simply providing scholarships,

71
00:04:43,589 --> 00:04:47,029
I want to give a second chance to young people...

72
00:04:47,759 --> 00:04:49,759
pushed to the edge by social prejudice.

73
00:04:50,669 --> 00:04:52,569
A practical and realistic...

74
00:04:53,139 --> 00:04:55,739
self-reliance program is currently in development.

75
00:05:03,309 --> 00:05:06,779
I was thinking about this while eating with Eun Seol yesterday.

76
00:05:08,679 --> 00:05:11,019
That correctional and rehabilitation program.

77
00:05:11,919 --> 00:05:12,949
Right.

78
00:05:13,319 --> 00:05:16,119
A reentry and reintegration program for prisoners?

79
00:05:16,319 --> 00:05:17,329
Yes.

80
00:05:17,859 --> 00:05:19,829
How about we select it as the new scholarship program...

81
00:05:19,899 --> 00:05:22,499
for our Cheongma Scholarship Foundation?

82
00:05:24,329 --> 00:05:27,899
It seems like a new program that breaks the mold.

83
00:05:28,569 --> 00:05:30,169
First, I would like you...

84
00:05:30,739 --> 00:05:32,939
to analyse existing rehabilitation programs...

85
00:05:33,409 --> 00:05:36,139
and prepare a rough budget.

86
00:05:38,679 --> 00:05:40,979
Sure, I'll get right on it.

87
00:05:44,089 --> 00:05:46,559
Ko Eun Seol has completely blinded her.

88
00:05:47,489 --> 00:05:48,519
What?

89
00:05:48,759 --> 00:05:50,489
A scholarship program for inmates?

90
00:05:52,929 --> 00:05:54,899
Just because people treat her like a queen,

91
00:05:54,959 --> 00:05:56,929
she thinks everyone is beneath her.

92
00:06:03,939 --> 00:06:04,969
Anyway,

93
00:06:05,439 --> 00:06:08,339
I feel stuck without someone to handle my grunt work.

94
00:06:20,189 --> 00:06:21,219
Hello.

95
00:06:21,989 --> 00:06:23,259
Director, it's me.

96
00:06:24,389 --> 00:06:25,529
Oh, right.

97
00:06:26,829 --> 00:06:29,659
Send me a few resumes like last time.

98
00:06:30,429 --> 00:06:33,199
(Head of Legal Affairs, Seo Hyun Jae)

99
00:06:39,669 --> 00:06:42,979
It seems to me like you're the one rattling her...

100
00:06:43,039 --> 00:06:44,879
just to ease your own guilt.

101
00:06:55,159 --> 00:06:56,159
Yes?

102
00:06:56,419 --> 00:06:59,529
Sir, the Planning Department meeting will start soon.

103
00:07:00,859 --> 00:07:03,059
Yes, I'll be right there.

104
00:07:09,069 --> 00:07:11,339
There's no problem with the trademark registration. However,

105
00:07:11,639 --> 00:07:14,279
when transferring patented technology to domestic factories,

106
00:07:14,479 --> 00:07:17,149
we must carefully draft a non-disclosure agreement first.

107
00:07:17,579 --> 00:07:20,519
The risk is too great if it is leaked in any way.

108
00:07:20,819 --> 00:07:22,679
Contracts are important, of course.

109
00:07:22,949 --> 00:07:25,289
But the field technicians are all domestic artisans...

110
00:07:25,349 --> 00:07:27,389
who've spent decades working together in this industry.

111
00:07:27,919 --> 00:07:29,759
Rather than simply binding them with paperwork,

112
00:07:29,819 --> 00:07:31,129
trust should come first.

113
00:07:32,459 --> 00:07:35,099
I'll check first for any unnecessary clauses.

114
00:07:35,159 --> 00:07:37,129
Actually, I'm not comfortable with that.

115
00:07:38,399 --> 00:07:41,339
Nothing is more dangerous in business than trusting people.

116
00:07:41,869 --> 00:07:43,609
We can't abandon legal protection...

117
00:07:43,669 --> 00:07:45,769
just because of your personal view, Mr. Cha.

118
00:07:47,839 --> 00:07:50,349
We'll proceed with the contract I reviewed.

119
00:07:50,779 --> 00:07:52,549
This isn't just a personal opinion,

120
00:07:53,179 --> 00:07:55,979
but a careful judgment from a manager who knows the field well.

121
00:08:14,099 --> 00:08:15,169
Attorney Seo,

122
00:08:15,899 --> 00:08:16,909
are you okay?

123
00:08:17,769 --> 00:08:19,469
You seemed really worked up earlier.

124
00:08:20,309 --> 00:08:21,609
Did I?

125
00:08:22,379 --> 00:08:23,379
Yes.

126
00:08:23,809 --> 00:08:25,909
I was surprised because I'd never seen...

127
00:08:25,979 --> 00:08:27,549
that side of you.

128
00:08:28,819 --> 00:08:29,819
Is that so?

129
00:08:31,719 --> 00:08:33,719
But it wasn't bad or anything.

130
00:08:34,159 --> 00:08:35,919
It's nice to see you turn into a professional...

131
00:08:36,319 --> 00:08:37,359
when you work.

132
00:08:40,699 --> 00:08:41,699
But by any chance,

133
00:08:42,899 --> 00:08:46,999
are things uncomfortable between you and Chief Cha?

134
00:08:47,539 --> 00:08:49,069
No. Not at all.

135
00:08:50,109 --> 00:08:51,509
There's no reason for that.

136
00:09:02,779 --> 00:09:04,649
Seok Jin, why are you so worked up today?

137
00:09:05,449 --> 00:09:07,859
- I'm not worked up. - Yes, you are.

138
00:09:08,689 --> 00:09:12,129
The meeting with Mr. Seo was just a formality at best,

139
00:09:12,829 --> 00:09:13,929
but you still got all worked up.

140
00:09:14,029 --> 00:09:15,129
As if.

141
00:09:16,329 --> 00:09:17,369
But you know what?

142
00:09:17,529 --> 00:09:19,129
My heart fluttered a bit watching you today.

143
00:09:19,729 --> 00:09:22,639
Watching my man work with such passion...

144
00:09:23,169 --> 00:09:24,539
You looked so sexy.

145
00:09:24,739 --> 00:09:26,239
I'd like to rest for five minutes.

146
00:09:26,609 --> 00:09:29,309
Rest? We need to eat lunch.

147
00:09:30,649 --> 00:09:31,809
What should we get?

148
00:09:32,909 --> 00:09:35,379
It looked like Ko Eun Seol was heading to lunch with Mr. Seo.

149
00:09:37,089 --> 00:09:39,649
Are they dating? All signs point to that.

150
00:09:39,789 --> 00:09:41,419
They're always attached at the hip.

151
00:09:42,759 --> 00:09:44,629
If that isn't an office romance, what is?

152
00:09:46,189 --> 00:09:49,059
Don't you get that vibe from them too?

153
00:09:51,369 --> 00:09:52,369
Let's head out for lunch.

154
00:09:52,869 --> 00:09:54,669
Sure. What should we have?

155
00:09:55,469 --> 00:09:56,539
I'm hungry.

156
00:10:02,579 --> 00:10:03,679
What are you doing?

157
00:10:04,109 --> 00:10:05,109
Oh, this?

158
00:10:05,509 --> 00:10:07,349
I'm going to teach Teun Teun when he gets back from the dojo.

159
00:10:08,449 --> 00:10:11,519
It's all about the angles, you see.

160
00:10:12,619 --> 00:10:15,219
The moves might look easy, but they're very detailed,

161
00:10:15,789 --> 00:10:17,159
so practice is the only way.

162
00:10:19,159 --> 00:10:21,159
People would think you're a taekwondo master.

163
00:10:21,359 --> 00:10:22,429
How did you know?

164
00:10:23,199 --> 00:10:24,399
I may not look like it,

165
00:10:24,469 --> 00:10:26,299
but I have a black belt in taekwondo.

166
00:10:26,939 --> 00:10:30,099
Something like Taegeuk 1 Jang is a piece of cake.

167
00:10:32,539 --> 00:10:33,939
Gosh, you're kicking up dust.

168
00:10:34,309 --> 00:10:35,939
If you're bored,

169
00:10:36,009 --> 00:10:37,379
please organise the inventory over there.

170
00:10:38,109 --> 00:10:39,109
Got it.

171
00:10:41,149 --> 00:10:43,149
Don't expect a bonus for that.

172
00:10:43,549 --> 00:10:44,989
There's no overtime pay either.

173
00:10:46,149 --> 00:10:47,859
I'm not doing it for the money.

174
00:10:48,689 --> 00:10:50,089
Then why are you doing it?

175
00:10:52,689 --> 00:10:54,599
So that Teun Teun doesn't lose confidence.

176
00:10:55,459 --> 00:10:58,099
When raising boys, physical development matters more...

177
00:10:58,169 --> 00:10:59,869
than focusing on their minds.

178
00:11:00,869 --> 00:11:03,239
Raising them to be active and strong...

179
00:11:03,669 --> 00:11:06,339
helps them grow tall and stay confident.

180
00:11:08,979 --> 00:11:11,549
Why are you so interested in someone else's son?

181
00:11:11,779 --> 00:11:12,879
It's not your place.

182
00:11:15,279 --> 00:11:16,349
Why else?

183
00:11:17,289 --> 00:11:18,419
He's adorable, that's why.

184
00:11:29,729 --> 00:11:31,699
Eun Seol, do you still have a lot left?

185
00:11:34,399 --> 00:11:35,939
Were you waiting for me?

186
00:11:36,969 --> 00:11:39,669
No. I had a lot of work today too,

187
00:11:40,539 --> 00:11:42,139
so I stopped by just in case.

188
00:11:44,379 --> 00:11:46,249
I was just about to head home.

189
00:11:47,619 --> 00:11:48,649
You're getting...

190
00:11:49,249 --> 00:11:50,949
your first paycheck today.

191
00:11:52,519 --> 00:11:53,889
Why don't we grab a bite?

192
00:11:54,659 --> 00:11:56,289
Actually, I'm planning...

193
00:11:56,359 --> 00:11:58,359
on having dinner with my family today.

194
00:11:59,059 --> 00:12:00,299
Oh, right.

195
00:12:01,459 --> 00:12:02,499
I didn't think of that.

196
00:12:03,129 --> 00:12:04,899
It's my very first paycheck,

197
00:12:05,329 --> 00:12:07,499
but this one feels extra special to me.

198
00:12:08,099 --> 00:12:10,439
It's the first paycheck I've earned with my own hands...

199
00:12:10,509 --> 00:12:11,809
since re-entering society.

200
00:12:12,709 --> 00:12:13,709
Of course.

201
00:12:14,379 --> 00:12:15,479
I think you really should...

202
00:12:15,479 --> 00:12:17,809
spend today with your family.

203
00:12:19,149 --> 00:12:20,149
Shall we?

204
00:12:38,899 --> 00:12:41,999
What's so important that you're calling us all out at bedtime?

205
00:12:43,339 --> 00:12:45,839
Well, I got my first paycheck.

206
00:12:46,739 --> 00:12:48,479
What, your paycheck?

207
00:12:48,909 --> 00:12:51,379
- How much did you get? - Mom, could you please...

208
00:12:52,679 --> 00:12:54,079
Has it already been a month?

209
00:12:54,419 --> 00:12:56,519
You've done such a great job, sweetie.

210
00:12:58,819 --> 00:13:01,319
Congratulations on your first paycheck, Eun Seol.

211
00:13:02,559 --> 00:13:04,759
They say if you spend your first paycheck like this,

212
00:13:05,329 --> 00:13:07,159
it brings in even more money.

213
00:13:08,159 --> 00:13:10,669
Since you were at it, you should've been more generous.

214
00:13:12,229 --> 00:13:14,269
Well, I'm good.

215
00:13:14,369 --> 00:13:15,799
I have 70 dollars to spend.

216
00:13:17,239 --> 00:13:18,539
I'm good too.

217
00:13:19,409 --> 00:13:20,779
How could I take that money?

218
00:13:21,309 --> 00:13:22,739
I already feel incredibly guilty.

219
00:13:23,009 --> 00:13:24,579
What's there to feel guilty about?

220
00:13:24,749 --> 00:13:26,609
Think about how much it cost to raise her.

221
00:13:27,219 --> 00:13:28,319
She's just getting started.

222
00:13:30,419 --> 00:13:31,749
Even if it's not a lot,

223
00:13:31,789 --> 00:13:34,719
you should keep giving us some every month.

224
00:13:34,719 --> 00:13:36,419
That's the least you can do.

225
00:13:42,629 --> 00:13:44,569
Give that back here! My gosh.

226
00:13:45,069 --> 00:13:46,129
Oh, my money.

227
00:13:46,699 --> 00:13:48,999
Come on, Mom, have a conscience.

228
00:13:49,069 --> 00:13:50,569
We're the ones who should be ashamed.

229
00:13:50,909 --> 00:13:52,139
Who do you think...

230
00:13:52,739 --> 00:13:54,239
put a roof over our heads?

231
00:13:54,509 --> 00:13:56,609
Exactly. Grandma, this isn't right.

232
00:13:56,839 --> 00:13:57,879
Out of everyone here,

233
00:13:58,379 --> 00:13:59,879
you're the most shameless.

234
00:14:00,079 --> 00:14:03,279
Sure. You must be happy your grandma is shameless.

235
00:14:03,349 --> 00:14:04,549
Happy now? Unbelievable.

236
00:14:07,589 --> 00:14:10,319
Eun Guk, Dad, just take it.

237
00:14:12,329 --> 00:14:13,329
But...

238
00:14:13,899 --> 00:14:14,929
I couldn't...

239
00:14:23,669 --> 00:14:24,669
Hey.

240
00:14:25,469 --> 00:14:26,539
I can't take this.

241
00:14:29,239 --> 00:14:32,379
Who said I'm just giving it to you? I'm going to get it all back.

242
00:14:33,679 --> 00:14:34,679
What?

243
00:14:34,949 --> 00:14:35,949
Later,

244
00:14:36,419 --> 00:14:40,089
when you get your first paycheck, I'm going to get it all back.

245
00:14:41,289 --> 00:14:44,729
Not from a part-time job, but once you get a real job,

246
00:14:45,259 --> 00:14:46,529
I'll get it all back.

247
00:14:47,329 --> 00:14:48,559
I'm going to get back twice as much, you know.

248
00:14:48,859 --> 00:14:51,069
Right, okay. Take it all back.

249
00:14:51,869 --> 00:14:53,029
Once I get settled,

250
00:14:53,399 --> 00:14:54,699
I'll pay you back first.

251
00:14:54,799 --> 00:14:55,799
Sure.

252
00:14:55,939 --> 00:14:58,609
So make sure you get on your feet, okay?

253
00:15:00,239 --> 00:15:02,339
All right. Just you wait.

254
00:15:17,929 --> 00:15:18,959
Hello?

255
00:15:19,359 --> 00:15:21,399
Eun Seol, it's me.

256
00:15:21,829 --> 00:15:23,799
Wait, Chairman Kim?

257
00:15:25,299 --> 00:15:27,469
Can you spare some time?

258
00:15:30,169 --> 00:15:31,669
I bet I surprised you.

259
00:15:32,809 --> 00:15:35,209
Yes, I was a little surprised.

260
00:15:36,639 --> 00:15:38,449
I'm sorry for calling you out so suddenly.

261
00:15:39,479 --> 00:15:41,319
We could've talked at the office,

262
00:15:41,919 --> 00:15:44,819
but I thought it'd be more comfortable here.

263
00:15:45,849 --> 00:15:47,559
No, it's fine.

264
00:15:49,719 --> 00:15:51,059
The reason I called you is this.

265
00:15:52,089 --> 00:15:54,129
Our Cheongma Scholarship Foundation...

266
00:15:55,199 --> 00:15:57,999
plans to support the inmate rehabilitation program.

267
00:15:59,099 --> 00:16:00,099
What?

268
00:16:02,069 --> 00:16:05,009
Since it's a rehabilitation program for inmates,

269
00:16:05,439 --> 00:16:06,709
there will be a lot of talk.

270
00:16:08,239 --> 00:16:09,439
I know it's a tough subject for you,

271
00:16:10,409 --> 00:16:13,249
but I wanted to ask for your advice.

272
00:16:15,349 --> 00:16:16,679
Actually, I'm a bit hesitant...

273
00:16:16,679 --> 00:16:20,019
because I didn't want this request to be a burden to you.

274
00:16:23,389 --> 00:16:24,389
I...

275
00:16:27,299 --> 00:16:29,799
To young people in the same situation as you,

276
00:16:30,569 --> 00:16:33,769
you could become another beacon of hope.

277
00:16:35,639 --> 00:16:37,869
Could you help us out?

278
00:16:42,839 --> 00:16:43,879
Sure.

279
00:16:44,379 --> 00:16:47,149
I may not be of much help, but I'll assist when needed.

280
00:16:50,649 --> 00:16:52,119
Thank you, Eun Seol.

281
00:17:02,099 --> 00:17:04,769
So, have you selected a new scholarship program?

282
00:17:04,969 --> 00:17:06,869
Yes, actually,

283
00:17:06,869 --> 00:17:08,699
Director Joo and I are planning it right now.

284
00:17:09,969 --> 00:17:14,279
We're preparing something unlike our usual programs,

285
00:17:14,679 --> 00:17:15,809
so you can look forward to it.

286
00:17:15,809 --> 00:17:19,549
This is the very first program under your leadership as Chairman.

287
00:17:19,879 --> 00:17:21,219
Don't go looking for something new...

288
00:17:21,279 --> 00:17:23,419
only to end up making a mess of things.

289
00:17:23,619 --> 00:17:24,989
Don't worry.

290
00:17:25,619 --> 00:17:29,459
I'll prepare it perfectly and convince you as well.

291
00:17:29,719 --> 00:17:31,129
Right, Director Joo?

292
00:17:31,859 --> 00:17:34,159
Yes, I'll make sure there aren't any issues.

293
00:17:46,409 --> 00:17:47,409
I'm off.

294
00:17:48,079 --> 00:17:49,679
- Mr. Seok Jin. - Yes?

295
00:17:50,409 --> 00:17:51,709
Take this with you.

296
00:17:52,709 --> 00:17:53,779
What's this?

297
00:17:54,349 --> 00:17:55,349
Tomatoes.

298
00:17:55,419 --> 00:17:57,349
They say tomatoes are good for your health.

299
00:17:59,249 --> 00:18:00,619
Thanks, Mom. I'll enjoy them.

300
00:18:01,359 --> 00:18:02,589
Hold on a second.

301
00:18:04,059 --> 00:18:06,229
This is for the nice lady.

302
00:18:07,029 --> 00:18:08,029
The nice lady?

303
00:18:08,559 --> 00:18:11,629
Yes. The nice lady needs to eat tomatoes, too.

304
00:18:11,999 --> 00:18:13,029
I see.

305
00:18:13,629 --> 00:18:15,339
It's fine, Mom. It can just be for me.

306
00:18:15,539 --> 00:18:16,869
No way.

307
00:18:16,939 --> 00:18:19,539
You have to give these to her. Okay?

308
00:18:20,169 --> 00:18:22,279
Have a good day, Mr. Seok Jin.

309
00:18:35,119 --> 00:18:36,119
What?

310
00:18:37,559 --> 00:18:39,559
But the nice lady should have some too.

311
00:18:52,339 --> 00:18:54,939
This tea works wonders for hangovers.

312
00:18:54,939 --> 00:18:57,949
Drinking it every now and then will help settle your stomach.

313
00:19:01,149 --> 00:19:02,279
Thanks, Director Joo.

314
00:19:04,549 --> 00:19:05,549
By the way,

315
00:19:05,919 --> 00:19:08,259
what exactly is the scholarship program...

316
00:19:08,319 --> 00:19:10,459
my wife is working on right now?

317
00:19:11,729 --> 00:19:14,259
It's a rehabilitation program designed...

318
00:19:14,259 --> 00:19:15,799
for incarcerated individuals.

319
00:19:17,469 --> 00:19:20,299
What? A rehabilitation program?

320
00:19:21,269 --> 00:19:23,539
I believe she was inspired after hearing about Ko Eun Seol...

321
00:19:23,599 --> 00:19:25,009
from the Design Team.

322
00:19:26,139 --> 00:19:29,039
What on earth does she think she's doing?

323
00:19:29,339 --> 00:19:31,209
Doesn't she care about the group's image?

324
00:19:31,479 --> 00:19:33,409
Especially right now,

325
00:19:33,479 --> 00:19:35,449
with all eyes on us for the new brand launch,

326
00:19:35,449 --> 00:19:37,319
she's supporting a rehabilitation program?

327
00:19:38,619 --> 00:19:40,919
It's still in the review stage.

328
00:19:43,859 --> 00:19:46,529
For now, Director Joo, you follow up on it...

329
00:19:46,959 --> 00:19:48,359
and report the situation to me frequently.

330
00:19:49,229 --> 00:19:50,969
Yes, I'll do that.

331
00:19:52,069 --> 00:19:53,129
You may go now.

332
00:20:00,639 --> 00:20:01,679
Director Joo,

333
00:20:02,939 --> 00:20:04,549
I can trust you, right?

334
00:20:05,879 --> 00:20:09,779
I know very well what you're worried about right now.

335
00:20:12,849 --> 00:20:16,359
I mean, you're never wrong with your choices.

336
00:20:17,359 --> 00:20:18,359
Honey!

337
00:20:21,459 --> 00:20:23,299
Honey, are you ready to go?

338
00:20:23,729 --> 00:20:25,829
Right, yes. Let's go.

339
00:20:33,409 --> 00:20:34,739
(2026 Cheongma Youth Stepping Stone Scholarship)

340
00:20:35,379 --> 00:20:36,379
Unbelievable.

341
00:20:37,309 --> 00:20:38,909
A positive influence?

342
00:20:42,079 --> 00:20:43,319
Who does she think she is?

343
00:20:45,849 --> 00:20:47,519
To a socialite who's only walked on a bed of roses,

344
00:20:47,589 --> 00:20:49,789
the whole world must look noble and beautiful.

345
00:20:51,729 --> 00:20:53,689
Someone who's never crawled at the bottom...

346
00:20:54,199 --> 00:20:56,059
is playing angel with just empty talk?

347
00:20:57,329 --> 00:20:59,669
Right, you've always been like that.

348
00:21:00,199 --> 00:21:02,799
Pretending to be kind, fragile, and innocent all by yourself.

349
00:21:04,569 --> 00:21:07,809
Fine, play angel all you want.

350
00:21:09,079 --> 00:21:10,479
I'll watch with my own two eyes...

351
00:21:10,849 --> 00:21:12,649
as your hypocrisy and arrogance...

352
00:21:13,279 --> 00:21:15,419
bring you down.

353
00:21:23,819 --> 00:21:27,559
How about we reinforce this section a bit more to improve airflow?

354
00:21:28,199 --> 00:21:29,199
Sure.

355
00:21:33,799 --> 00:21:34,799
This side too.

356
00:21:38,909 --> 00:21:40,569
I'm so annoyed.

357
00:21:41,579 --> 00:21:43,139
What is it this time?

358
00:21:43,239 --> 00:21:44,449
It's Ko Eun Seol.

359
00:21:44,779 --> 00:21:46,509
I should've never accepted her from the start.

360
00:21:47,079 --> 00:21:48,179
Using work as an excuse,

361
00:21:48,179 --> 00:21:50,249
she's sticking to Seok Jin like glue.

362
00:21:51,189 --> 00:21:53,219
I told you not to act so emotionally.

363
00:21:53,649 --> 00:21:55,889
How can I not be emotional?

364
00:21:56,189 --> 00:21:59,059
If your man was glued to another woman,

365
00:21:59,129 --> 00:22:00,129
could you tolerate that?

366
00:22:00,689 --> 00:22:02,929
Chief Cha will only pull away more if you act like this.

367
00:22:03,599 --> 00:22:05,299
You need to use his weakness against him instead.

368
00:22:05,999 --> 00:22:07,099
His weakness?

369
00:22:07,399 --> 00:22:10,169
Even Ms. Park has already fallen for Ko Eun Seol's tricks.

370
00:22:11,909 --> 00:22:15,379
Then take So Yeon out shopping or something.

371
00:22:16,509 --> 00:22:17,579
Shopping?

372
00:22:18,209 --> 00:22:20,949
But I hate hanging out with Ms. Park.

373
00:22:21,349 --> 00:22:23,419
You're doing it for Seok Jin to see.

374
00:22:24,849 --> 00:22:27,319
No man is going to turn away a woman who takes his mom out.

375
00:22:27,889 --> 00:22:31,529
Then, when it's just you and her, intimidate her or something...

376
00:22:31,859 --> 00:22:33,659
to get her to behave.

377
00:22:38,469 --> 00:22:40,599
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

378
00:22:44,239 --> 00:22:46,039
Seok Jin, what's Ms. Park doing tomorrow?

379
00:22:47,009 --> 00:22:48,809
Unless something special pops up, she'll probably be at daycare. Why?

380
00:22:48,909 --> 00:22:50,909
I want to go shopping with her tomorrow.

381
00:22:51,079 --> 00:22:52,209
I'll do that.

382
00:22:54,519 --> 00:22:55,579
Will my mother like that?

383
00:22:56,319 --> 00:22:59,019
Why? Does she hate being around me?

384
00:22:59,549 --> 00:23:01,289
She's just not all that comfortable around you.

385
00:23:02,059 --> 00:23:03,159
The feeling is mutual.

386
00:23:03,659 --> 00:23:06,989
Still, I'm putting in an effort since she's my future mother-in-law.

387
00:23:08,359 --> 00:23:09,559
All right, I'll let her know.

388
00:23:10,359 --> 00:23:11,429
Should I go pick her up?

389
00:23:11,499 --> 00:23:13,329
No, the daycare staff will handle it.

390
00:23:14,069 --> 00:23:15,069
Oh, right.

391
00:23:15,669 --> 00:23:16,969
You know how careful you have to be...

392
00:23:17,039 --> 00:23:18,409
when my mom goes somewhere new, right?

393
00:23:18,909 --> 00:23:19,909
Of course.

394
00:23:23,039 --> 00:23:26,949
Yes, go ahead and try it.

395
00:23:29,449 --> 00:23:30,519
How is it?

396
00:23:31,389 --> 00:23:32,719
Wait, what?

397
00:23:33,349 --> 00:23:35,959
I mean, this taste is out of this world.

398
00:23:37,259 --> 00:23:38,529
Tell me the truth.

399
00:23:39,229 --> 00:23:41,899
Were you trying to kill your mom with this?

400
00:23:42,499 --> 00:23:44,599
Wait, is it that bad?

401
00:23:45,229 --> 00:23:47,399
You're both faking it, aren't you?

402
00:23:53,739 --> 00:23:56,909
How can cooked squid possibly taste this bad?

403
00:23:57,209 --> 00:23:58,779
I was planning to get a loan...

404
00:23:59,609 --> 00:24:03,179
and start a restaurant to take some pressure off Eun Seol.

405
00:24:03,249 --> 00:24:04,349
Unbelievable.

406
00:24:04,589 --> 00:24:07,319
You'll end up killing people trying to help Eun Seol.

407
00:24:07,589 --> 00:24:12,289
Dad, this tastes like a crime against humanity.

408
00:24:12,789 --> 00:24:13,789
Hey.

409
00:24:14,829 --> 00:24:16,729
Leave it, I'll just do it myself.

410
00:24:18,569 --> 00:24:19,729
You're no better, Grandma.

411
00:24:19,799 --> 00:24:21,769
Why do you think Dad started cooking?

412
00:24:21,839 --> 00:24:24,739
Dad had to step in because your cooking was so bad.

413
00:24:25,609 --> 00:24:28,539
When you try to cook something in the kitchen,

414
00:24:29,779 --> 00:24:31,749
I get goosebumps all over.

415
00:24:31,749 --> 00:24:34,749
Oh, please, I'm still better than your dad.

416
00:24:34,819 --> 00:24:35,819
Move.

417
00:24:35,819 --> 00:24:38,419
Mom, why? What are you doing?

418
00:24:39,289 --> 00:24:40,289
But...

419
00:24:41,319 --> 00:24:43,619
- Dad, I leave the rest to you. - My goodness.

420
00:24:44,019 --> 00:24:45,529
You always do that when things get sticky.

421
00:24:46,029 --> 00:24:49,959
Darn it, this is a mess.

422
00:24:50,499 --> 00:24:52,529
- Oh, man. - What's with them?

423
00:24:53,529 --> 00:24:54,599
Whatever.

424
00:25:15,589 --> 00:25:17,889
Sweetie, you've been working so hard lately, haven't you?

425
00:25:18,659 --> 00:25:20,589
I'll get back on my feet soon...

426
00:25:20,929 --> 00:25:24,899
and give you a generous allowance.

427
00:25:26,269 --> 00:25:28,969
I'm always thankful, and I love you.

428
00:25:56,999 --> 00:25:59,969
- Mr. Seok Jin. - Mom, did you wait long?

429
00:25:59,969 --> 00:26:00,969
Yes.

430
00:26:02,299 --> 00:26:05,309
You're only hanging out with me today, Mother.

431
00:26:05,809 --> 00:26:06,839
But why?

432
00:26:07,509 --> 00:26:08,579
What about Mr. Seok Jin?

433
00:26:09,279 --> 00:26:12,979
Seok Jin has to work. He's a very busy man.

434
00:26:15,049 --> 00:26:16,049
Really?

435
00:26:16,219 --> 00:26:17,219
Yes.

436
00:26:18,019 --> 00:26:21,519
Consider today a special date for you and Hae Ra.

437
00:26:21,789 --> 00:26:22,789
Are you excited?

438
00:26:28,099 --> 00:26:29,099
Don't you want to go?

439
00:26:32,599 --> 00:26:33,599
Mom, please.

440
00:26:37,269 --> 00:26:40,809
Go with Hae Ra today and buy lots of things you like.

441
00:26:41,409 --> 00:26:42,409
Okay?

442
00:26:44,309 --> 00:26:46,379
Let's go, Mother. Don't worry, Seok Jin.

443
00:26:46,479 --> 00:26:48,779
I'll take her home after we're done shopping.

444
00:26:49,219 --> 00:26:50,849
- Okay, be careful. - Don't worry.

445
00:26:52,289 --> 00:26:53,289
Here.

446
00:26:55,859 --> 00:26:57,559
- Have fun. - Let's go, Mother.

447
00:27:09,399 --> 00:27:12,239
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

448
00:27:18,179 --> 00:27:20,109
Hello, this is Joo Mi Ran.

449
00:27:20,249 --> 00:27:22,479
What? Joo Mi Ran?

450
00:27:25,219 --> 00:27:26,319
Who is this?

451
00:27:26,319 --> 00:27:28,919
Joo Ae Sook, have you been well?

452
00:27:29,289 --> 00:27:32,889
It's me. Your husband, An Guk Chan.

453
00:27:48,339 --> 00:27:50,909
Ms. Park, how about this one?

454
00:27:52,849 --> 00:27:53,849
I don't like it.

455
00:27:55,649 --> 00:27:57,619
Your taste is so tacky.

456
00:27:59,719 --> 00:28:00,789
What did you say?

457
00:28:01,189 --> 00:28:02,559
It's nothing.

458
00:28:03,359 --> 00:28:06,559
Then how about this pink one? It looks very you.

459
00:28:07,159 --> 00:28:09,159
I said I don't like it.

460
00:28:10,659 --> 00:28:11,929
You've got to be kidding me.

461
00:28:12,399 --> 00:28:14,069
Then what do you want me to do?

462
00:28:18,609 --> 00:28:20,309
Bring out a few more like this.

463
00:28:21,239 --> 00:28:22,679
Sure, right this way.

464
00:28:34,659 --> 00:28:36,919
Hey, it's the nice lady.

465
00:28:39,129 --> 00:28:40,589
Ms. Park, where are you...

466
00:28:51,409 --> 00:28:52,409
Miss!

467
00:28:54,369 --> 00:28:55,409
Nice lady!

468
00:28:55,679 --> 00:28:57,039
Excuse me, I'm sorry to interrupt,

469
00:28:57,439 --> 00:28:59,379
I'm sorry to interrupt, but it looks like...

470
00:28:59,379 --> 00:29:01,079
the lady you were with just left.

471
00:29:05,789 --> 00:29:07,989
Mind your own business and get back to work.

472
00:29:08,919 --> 00:29:10,859
Right. Of course.

473
00:29:18,829 --> 00:29:19,829
Nice lady!

474
00:29:23,939 --> 00:29:26,409
Hold on. Nice lady!

475
00:29:26,709 --> 00:29:27,809
Nice lady.

476
00:29:30,139 --> 00:29:32,649
Nice lady!

477
00:30:08,319 --> 00:30:11,449
(A Trap Called Desire)

478
00:30:12,249 --> 00:30:13,719
You have to find him as soon as possible.

479
00:30:13,789 --> 00:30:16,589
Is he an ex-boyfriend who ran off with your money?

480
00:30:17,259 --> 00:30:20,729
Chief Cha even has a sick mom. Are you really ready to marry him?

481
00:30:20,729 --> 00:30:23,459
I think you should make it clear to him this time.

482
00:30:23,529 --> 00:30:25,369
What else? It's one of our couple rings.

483
00:30:25,369 --> 00:30:27,629
I wanted to get something a bit more flashy,

484
00:30:27,899 --> 00:30:30,439
but Seok Jin doesn't really enjoy the attention.

485
00:30:30,699 --> 00:30:33,139
I completely understand how you feel, Eun Seol.

486
00:30:33,539 --> 00:30:36,639
I didn't know you'd care for me this much, Ms. Joo.

487
00:30:36,639 --> 00:30:38,309
I thought if I just looked the other way,

488
00:30:38,309 --> 00:30:39,979
Ms. Park would disappear somewhere.

489
00:30:40,049 --> 00:30:41,879
I'm sorry, this is all on me.

490
00:30:41,979 --> 00:30:43,619
I'll do better.
